+# Saved shortlist verification recipe
+
+Scope: shortlist plus the connected search/story paths in this app. Tested source: `3ed7fc8` plus the source hashes in [evidence/shortlist/source-state.json](evidence/shortlist/source-state.json). This recipe is implemented by [shortlist-browser-test.mjs](shortlist-browser-test.mjs). Current results and limitations live in [records/experiment.md#saved-shortlist](records/experiment.md#saved-shortlist).
+
+## Owned local run
+
+Run from `experiments/cafe-personality-v2` with the existing installed dependencies. `npm ci` is only needed for a fresh checkout. No account or seed service is required; the six curated cafés are bundled.
+
+```sh
+npm test
+npm run build
+node node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js --host 127.0.0.1 --port 5181 --strictPort
+```
+
+Keep that server process owned by this terminal. A busy port is a setup conflict: choose another port and pass its URL as `BASE_URL` to the browser command. In another terminal from the app directory:
+
+```sh
+PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH='/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome' BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5181 node shortlist-browser-test.mjs
+```
+
+Other environments can omit the executable override when Playwright Chromium is installed. The script creates isolated browser contexts, verifies six search rows as readiness, closes its browser in `finally`, and preserves screenshots, traces and observations under `evidence/shortlist/`. Stop only your Vite process with Ctrl-C after success or failure. A run passes when the command exits 0 and prints its final PASS; screenshot presence alone is insufficient.
+
+## Feature map
+
+| Path | Start and controls | Observable result |
+|---|---|---|
+| Empty and discover | Fresh context → `Shortlist (0/3)` → `Discover cafés` | Empty guidance, focused heading, all six search rows |
+| Search save and duplicate | Focus first café row, Enter → focus `Save to shortlist`, Enter twice → Escape | Exactly one saved café; `Saved to shortlist` is unavailable; opener regains focus |
+| Capacity | Save Nylon, Apartment, Tiong Hoe → open Alchemist · The Mill → Enter on save | Clear 3-of-3 explanation; no fourth selection; `View shortlist` works |
+| Compare | `View shortlist` | Three cards, names, neighbourhoods, coffee, brews, addresses and exact Google Maps query; focused heading |
+| Remove and replace | `Remove Apartment Coffee` → `Discover more cafés` → save The Mill | Focus moves to next remove control; replacement persists |
+| Refresh | Reload → `Shortlist (3/3)` | Local storage contains nylon, tionghoe, mill and three corresponding cards |
+| Remove all | Remove each visible café | Heading regains focus; discovery action remains usable |
+| Existing search | Apartment + Selegie + Espresso → `Reset filters` | Empty filtered result then all cafés |
+| Story entry | `Your café story` → `Step inside`; quiet corner, Espresso, save a seat, golden hour; Continue after each | Three existing matches; first result can be saved; returning and `Change my choices` retains the chosen seat |
+| Damaged storage | Set key `sidequest-shortlist-v1` to malformed JSON, non-array, or unknown/duplicate/excess IDs then reload | Empty or first three unique known IDs, normalized back to storage |
+| Storage failure | Isolated context blocks localStorage getter or throws on writes | Saving/removal still work this visit; visible persistence-unavailable notice in detail and shortlist |
+| Responsive/focus | Main journey at 1440×1000 and 390×844 | No page overflow, readable comparison/actions and capacity dialog; native dialog and removal focus verified |
+
+Automated assertions cover each row. Inspect `comparison-1440.png`, `comparison-390.png`, and `capacity-390.png` for spacing, wrapping and label legibility. Traces `journey-1440.zip` and `journey-390.zip` retain interactions. The original motion/video recipe remains `browser-test.mjs` and was not rerun for this change; no animation or scene code changed. Uncovered: physical devices, Safari/Firefox, cross-tab synchronization, external directions destination availability and subjective user acceptance. No production actions.
