+## Saved shortlist — 18 Nov 2026
+
+**Ready for Verification.** Parent-assigned, user-authorized local feature trial; accountable human owner is the requesting user, with Cedar responsible only for this app and verification artifacts. Parent coordinates independent review. Source brief: `/tmp/cafe-shortlist-study/brief.md`, relayed in the `/root/cafe_cedar` task: “keep a few promising cafes and compare them before choosing one”; maximum three unique cafés, save from search/story details, compare name/neighbourhood/coffee/brews/address/directions, remove/replace, usable empty/capacity states, local ID persistence with malformed/unknown/duplicate/excess handling, storage failure notice, existing story/search/data, keyboard/focus and 390px/desktop usability. No publication, merge or commit was authorized in this worker assignment.
+
+Used/read paths: `AGENTS.md`, `NORTHSTAR.md`, `README.md`, `workflow.md`, `docs/workflows/deliver-change.md`, `docs/contracts/workflow-context.md`; `skills/implementation/implement-increments/SKILL.md` (bounded implementation/check cycles), `skills/verification/exercise-user-journey/SKILL.md` and its journey template (owned browser path/evidence), `skills/verification/verify-change/SKILL.md` (whole-brief author assessment), `skills/maintenance/maintain-user-journeys/SKILL.md` (existing-map inspection; no shortlist recipe existed, so establish one under exercise-user-journey). No suitable local visual design specialist was used; bounded fallback reuses this app's palette, typography, buttons and discovery layout, with rendered checks. Subjective design acceptance remains with the user.
+
+Decisions: a persistent navigation count opens a full-page comparison, with three desktop cards and stacked mobile cards. Save belongs in the shared detail dialog, covering both entry points without duplicate code. Native dialog focus restoration stays intact; opening comparison focuses its heading, removing focuses the next/previous removal or heading when empty. Keep save controls focusable with `aria-disabled` and an explicit guard so success/capacity stays keyboard-readable. Store only IDs under `sidequest-shortlist-v1`; normalize on load; failed storage does not roll back session state and is explained wherever shortlist saving/viewing occurs. Cross-tab synchronization was not requested. No dependencies or curated café/story facts changed.
